**Definition 7.1 (binding and public inputs).** The immutable target binding
is the exact ten-field tuple

$$
b=[\mathsf{unary74maskcontour},U(H_0),r_{\rm seed},r_{\rm boot},
       r_{\rm code},U(p),U(c),U(k),\varrho,\theta].
$$

The layout literal is binary `01010100`. The seed/boot/code entries are
the complete authentic acquired origin/version/capture bindings, not
numerals interpreted as permission. $\theta$ is the actual target
version/raw-installation phase. $\varrho$ is ARC's complete occurrence/
request-origin tuple. No seed contents, input word, endpoint, meter or
history is appended to $b$.

`PublicCode` consists of the fixed original graph/boot/prior/controller
parameters, $L$, the actually acquired $\Delta(G_\circ)$, corresponding
installation serialization and the fixed compiler/layout conventions.
It excludes variable manifest seed contents, request reservoirs, package
$I_k$ and the acquired Image. Its own code is not assumed physically present
at an older pre-capture target: its fixed later code parameter determines
the canonical supply, whose construction replay still performs only at
the actual rows. Later code/package references are checked against current
immutable acquired records; target fields are checked against the derived
old prefix. Later origins are not required to exist at an earlier cut.

More precisely, at an acquired-Zero target check its actual $\xi,H_0,k$,
version/raw phase, old unified count $m$ and producer-local request
references at the recognized $F^A$ occurrence. Resolve those same complete
request references through the later acquired origin copies. The unified
row's later delivery origin in $\varrho$ is checked in the frozen acquired
cover chain, not demanded inside the earlier Zero state. The cover/package
creation references and current invocation are likewise current-service
checks. These tests never substitute future origin payload for the body's
missing seed/input material.

Write $\mathcal Z_\circ$ for the subset of $\mathcal C_\circ$ consisting of
target prefixes actually selected by that acquired strict-Zero route.
The service decoder's positive domain is an authentic view of
$h\in\mathcal Z_\circ$ with its corresponding acquired $b$. The shape
inverses on $\mathcal R_\circ$ and input-complete semantic replay on
$\mathcal C_\circ$ do not assert a current acquired binding, selector or
converter invocation for every member of those larger domains.

